### 6. Graph Feature Computation Needs More Specificity (Section 5.1)

The graph features row in the table says "computed periodically (e.g., every 15 min)" but doesn't address the fact that graph computation at scale is **expensive** and the 15-min cadence may be unrealistic:

```markdown
#### Graph feature architecture (refined)

Two-tier approach:
1. **Pre-computed graph metrics** (degree centrality, PageRank, community ID per 
   entity) — computed via GraphFrames on a **dedicated Databricks job cluster** 
   every **1 hour** (not 15 min — community detection and centrality on even a 
   modest entity graph takes 10–20 min), materialized to the offline/online 
   feature store as slowly-changing features.
2. **Real-time local graph queries** — for inference-time features like 
   "how many distinct customers have used this device in the last 24h," use 
   **Azure Cosmos DB (Gremlin API)** with a 1-hop traversal (bounded query cost). 
   The entity graph in Cosmos is updated by a streaming Databricks job that 
   writes edges as transactions flow through Silver.

This avoids the trap of trying to do full graph recomputation at streaming speed 
while still giving the model fresh relational signals.
```

