### 10. Decision Threshold Calibration (Section 8.3)

The decision thresholds (0.10, 0.60, 0.90) are presented as fixed values. Add:

```markdown
> **Note:** These thresholds are initial values and must be tuned on historical 
> data using cost-sensitive analysis:
> - Cost of a false negative (missed fraud) ≈ average fraud loss amount
> - Cost of a false positive (blocking legitimate) ≈ customer lifetime value 
>   impact + support cost
> - Cost of step-up (friction) ≈ conversion drop rate × average transaction value
>
> Thresholds should be stored as **configuration in Azure App Configuration** 
> (not hardcoded), versioned, and adjustable by fraud-ops without redeployment. 
> Threshold changes should be logged as audit events.
```

